Description: Use a plan to run the same analysis function over many sets of
    arguments, or to run different functions on the same data. A plan holds
    the data sources, the argument sets and the functions. Running
    the plan loads the data once and passes it to every analysis, in sequence
    or in parallel. Typical uses are one method applied across strata such as
    locations or age groups, or across exposures and outcomes, and the tables
    and figures of a report.
